-county"],["ARC or PLC in Navarro County","/arc-plc/texas/navarro-county"],["PRF calculator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 11 grids runs 75 years, from 1951 to 2025, and September to October came in under 90% of normal in 41 of them, more than any other pair. In 2025 the middle ran 202% of normal in June to July and 58% in September to October. So far in 2026, February to March came in at 39% of normal on the middle. Grid 14236 had its driest year in 1963, at 52% of normal.</p>"}
